# ASIP reboot survival (t3)

- **Timestamp:** 2026-07-29
- **Host:** t3 (`ssh t3 -p 80`)

## Incident

After OS reboot at **05:01 UTC**, browsers showed **"Failed to fetch"** on Your IP / IP pages because `asip-api.xaigrok.ir` had no healthy backend.

| Service | Restart policy | Created | Started after reboot | Survived? |
|---------|----------------|---------|----------------------|-----------|
| haproxy | unless-stopped | 2026-07-17 | ~05:03 | Yes (same container) |
| asip-postgres | unless-stopped | 2026-07-29 05:17 | ~05:18 | Recreated by deploy |
| asip-api | unless-stopped | 2026-07-29 05:18 | ~05:18 | Recreated by deploy |
| asip-webui | unless-stopped | 2026-07-29 05:22 | ~05:22 | Recreated by deploy |

HAProxy logs during the gap: `be_asip_api` DOWN → DNS error → connection refused → UP once API returned.

External networks present: `t3-net`, `asip-net`, `asip-webui-net`.

Compose files on host: `/home/cloud-admin/docker/asip`, `/home/cloud-admin/docker/asip-webui`.

## Rules for survival

1. Keep `restart: unless-stopped` on postgres, asip-api, asip-webui, haproxy.
2. Do **not** run `docker compose down` before host reboot (removes containers; they cannot auto-restart).
3. Prefer `docker compose up -d` without wiping named containers/volumes.
4. Ensure Docker is enabled on boot: `systemctl is-enabled docker` → `enabled`.
5. Networks `t3-net`, `asip-net`, `asip-webui-net` must exist before compose up.

## After OS reboot — verify

```bash
ssh t3 -p 80

docker ps --filter name=asip --filter name=haproxy --format 'table {{.Names}}\t{{.Status}}'
docker inspect asip-api asip-webui haproxy --format '{{.Name}} Created={{.Created}} Restart={{.HostConfig.RestartPolicy.Name}}'
curl -sS -m 8 -o /dev/null -w 'api=%{http_code}\n' https://asip-api.xaigrok.ir/api/v1/health
curl -sS -m 8 -o /dev/null -w 'ui=%{http_code}\n' https://asip.xaigrok.ir/
```

Healthy survival: **Created** timestamps stay old; only **Started** updates.

## If asip stack is missing after reboot

Redeploy both stacks with existing scripts (from each repo on your workstation):

```powershell
# as-ip API + postgres
.\.armin\docker-scripts\run-on-docker-server.ps1

# asip-webui
.\.armin\docker-scripts\run-on-docker-server.ps1
```

On the server, compose dirs are:

- `/home/cloud-admin/docker/asip`
- `/home/cloud-admin/docker/asip-webui`

Example reconcile without a full image rebuild (if images already exist):

```bash
cd /home/cloud-admin/docker/asip && docker compose up -d
cd /home/cloud-admin/docker/asip-webui && docker compose up -d
```

## UI resilience

asip-webui `asIpClient` retries transient network failures (3 attempts, short backoff) and shows:

> API unreachable — service may still be starting after a server restart.
